//! Usenet engine: one NNTP connection pool shared by streaming reads and imports, with
//! provider priority tiers and per-purpose workloads.
//!
//! `vendor` holds the infinidysk engine crates and SuperFork lifts, regenerated by a
//! script and never edited by hand. The modules beside it are the facade consumers use:
//! [`Engine`] imports an NZB once, persists its layout under the data directory so a
//! restart reopens any output without touching providers, and opens outputs as
//! seekable readers that share one in-flight fetch per article.
//!
//! A release is keyed by [`ReleaseKey`], a hash of each file's first message-id, so the
//! same post fetched from different indexers or re-encoded NZBs maps to one release, and
//! its outputs are numbered over their sorted paths rather than NZB order. An NZB that
//! lists a different set of files (one indexer drops the PAR2 files, or a file's first
//! segment) hashes to a different key, so the same post can then exist as two releases.

